    {
      "fileName": "elver-pet.json",
      "id": "aBa7dGY2TuDE4R7A",
      "name": "Elver Pet",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "aBa7dGY2TuDE4R7A",
        "folder": "uRFIvEiCaUKlRZQU",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Elver Pet",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "ancestry",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>Athamarus have bonded with eels more closely than any other fish. You have formed a strong connection with a young eel that serves as your pet. Typically, these eels are tended until they grow large enough to serve as a mount. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Pet] general feat. Instead of the normal choice of pet abilities, your eel has aquatic, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.familiar-abilities.Item.Fast Movement], and the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.familiar-abilities.Item.Damage Avoidance] familiar ability for Reflex saves. The aquatic ability means it gains the aquatic trait, breathes water instead of air, and has a swim Speed instead of a land Speed.</p>\n<p>When you aren't in an aquatic environment, you can easily carry your pet eel around in a small water-filled globe that has light Bulk.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Howl of the Wild"
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "GrantItem",
              "uuid": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Pet"
            }
          ],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "athamaru"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 1,
